# Ask the perception side: where should the machine go next?
#
# The request is deliberately empty. The caller is a control-side node reacting to
# a machine request; it has no information the perception side needs, and keeping
# the request empty is what lets completely unrelated implementations satisfy this
# interface.
---
# Target position in SI units (metres), in the frame named by header.frame_id.
# See units.py: everything on the ROS side of this system is metres, per REP-103.
geometry_msgs/PointStamped target

# False if no valid target could be produced this cycle.
bool success

# True when the source has nothing left to offer (bin empty, tray cleared, ...).
# The caller should stop requesting until the source is replenished.
bool source_exhausted
